ront_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>stance<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>stance<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: take a stance \/ adopt a stance \/ firm stance \/ defensive stance<\/span><\/p><p>similar: posture \/ position \/ viewpoint \/ attitude<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: indecision \/ wavering \/ flexibility<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":2,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-08","reviewed_on":"2026-06-10","due_at":"2026-06-10T18:27:13+00:00","previous_state":{"state":"learning","due_at":"2026-06-09T20:01:06+00:00","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":2,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-08","reviewed_on":"2026-06-09"}},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"45 perc","good":"1 \u00f3ra","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-06-10T17:54:54+00:00"},{"id":51416,"front":"<p>The company decided to _______ a major new construction project, despite the economic uncertainty. <em>(elv\u00e1llal \/ belekezd)<\/em><\/p><p>He had to _______ a long and difficult journey to reach his destination. <em>(megtesz \/ v\u00e9grehajt)<\/em><\/p><p>The government will _______ a thorough investigation into the allegations of corruption. <em>(ind\u00edt \/ foganatos\u00edt)<\/em><\/p><p>Are you willing to _______ the responsibility for this decision? <em>(mag\u00e1ra v\u00e1llal \/ felv\u00e1llal)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">elv\u00e1llal \/ megtesz \/ belekezd<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): elutas\u00edt \/ visszautas\u00edt \/ lemond<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a project = projektet elv\u00e1llal (pl. They will _______ a new research project next month.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a task = feladatot elv\u00e1llal\/v\u00e9grehajt (pl. It&#039;s a difficult task, but someone has to _______ it.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a journey = utat megtesz (pl. Explorers often _______ perilous journeys.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a responsibility = felel\u0151ss\u00e9get felv\u00e1llal (pl. He was reluctant to _______ such a huge responsibility.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ an investigation = vizsg\u00e1latot ind\u00edt\/lefolytat (pl. The police decided to _______ an immediate investigation.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>undertake<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>undertaking<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>undertake<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: undertake a project \/ undertake a task \/ undertake a journey \/ undertake responsibility<\/span><\/p><p>similar: commence \/ embark on \/ perform \/ assume<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: abandon \/ forego \/ decline<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"undertake","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":2,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-06","reviewed_on":"2026-06-10","due_at":"2026-06-10T18:12:18+00:00","previous_state":{"state":"learning","due_at":"2026-06-09T19:27:07+00:00","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":1,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-06","reviewed_on":"2026-06-09"}},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"45 perc","good":"1 \u00f3ra","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-06-10T20:41:34+00:00"},{"id":51436,"front":"<p>The sun will _______ in the east, bringing a new day. <em>(felkel \/ emelkedik)<\/em><\/p><p>We need to see a significant _______ in sales figures this quarter. <em>(n\u00f6veked\u00e9s \/ emelked\u00e9s)<\/em><\/p><p>A new political party began to _______ to power, promising radical changes. <em>(felemelkedik \/ hatalomra jut)<\/em><\/p><p>A feeling of dread began to _______ in her as she walked through the dark forest. <em>(felt\u00f6r \/ n\u00f6vekszik)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">emelkedik \/ n\u00f6vekszik \/ felkel \/ emelked\u00e9s<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): cs\u00f6kken \/ esik \/ s\u00fcllyed<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 the sun will _______ = a nap felkel (pl. The sun will _______ early tomorrow morning.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _______ in prices = \u00e1remelked\u00e9s (pl. We expect a sharp _______ in prices next month.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ to power = hatalomra jut (pl. He managed to _______ to power through popular support.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to give _______ to something = teret ad valaminek, \u00e9letre kel (pl. The new policy could give _______ to further debate.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ from the ashes = felt\u00e1mad a hamvaib\u00f3l (pl. After the defeat, the team vowed to _______ from the ashes.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>rise<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>risen<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>rise<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>rise<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: rise and fall \/ rise in temperature \/ rise to the occasion \/ rise from bed<\/span><\/p><p>similar: ascend \/ climb \/ increase \/ mount<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: fall \/ drop \/ descend<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"rise","study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":5,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-09","reviewed_on":"2026-06-10","due_at":"2026-06-11T01:50:23+00:00","previous_state":{"state":"learning","due_at":"2026-06-10T19:44:21+00:00","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,