gh a series of ancient rituals. <em>(felvesz \/ beavat)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">bevezet \/ felvesz \/ beiktat<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): kiz\u00e1r \/ elt\u00e1vol\u00edt \/ elutas\u00edt<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ someone into a position = valakit poz\u00edci\u00f3ba beiktat (pl. The president will _______ the new minister into his role next week.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ someone into a club\/organization = valakit klubba\/szervezetbe felvesz (pl. They decided to _______ several new members into the chess club.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a new system\/policy = \u00faj rendszert\/politik\u00e1t bevezet (pl. The government plans to _______ a new tax policy.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ someone into the military = valakit katonai szolg\u00e1latba bevon (pl. He was _______ into the army right after high school.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>induct<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>induction<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>induct<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: induct into \/ induct new members \/ induct a system \/ induct a policy<\/span><\/p><p>similar: admit \/ initiate \/ install \/ introduce<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: expel \/ exclude \/ reject<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"induct\ninduction","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":2,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-06","reviewed_on":"2026-06-10","due_at":"2026-06-10T18:10:00+00:00","previous_state":{"state":"learning","due_at":"2026-06-09T19:27:09+00:00","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":1,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-06","reviewed_on":"2026-06-09"}},"previews":