_______ upper lip, refusing to complain. <em>(rezzen\u00e9stelen \/ rend\u00edthetetlen)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">merev \/ kem\u00e9ny \/ rideg<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): hajl\u00e9kony \/ rugalmas \/ laza<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _______ drink = er\u0151s ital (pl. He needed a _______ drink after a long day.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 keep a _______ upper lip = rezzen\u00e9stelen arccal viselkedik (pl. Despite the bad news, she managed to keep a _______ upper lip.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ competition = kem\u00e9ny verseny (pl. They faced _______ competition in the tech industry.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _______ breeze = er\u0151s szell\u0151 (pl. A _______ breeze rustled through the trees.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>stiff<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>stiff<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>stiffly<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>stiffness<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: stiff neck \/ stiff drink \/ stiff competition \/ stiff breeze<\/span><\/p><p>similar: rigid \/ inflexible \/ firm \/ harsh<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: flexible \/ loose \/ pliable<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-10","reviewed_on":"2026-06-10","due_at":"2026-06-10T17:45:57+00:00","previous_state":{"state":"learning","due_at":"2026-06-10T13:35:44+00:00","interval":0,"ease_factor":250,"repetitions":0,"lapses":0,"learning_step":0,"is_leech":false,"introduced_on":"2026-06-10","reviewed_on":"2026-06-10"}},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-06-11T16:08:41+00:00"},{"id":51434,"front":"<p>After realizing she left her keys at the cafe, she had to _______ her steps all the way back. <em>(visszamegy \/ visszak\u00f6vet)<\/em><\/p><p>Detectives often have to _______ a suspect&#039;s movements to build a timeline of events. <em>(nyomon k\u00f6vet \/ felder\u00edt)<\/em><\/p><p>To understand the current economic crisis, we must _______ the historical factors that led to it. <em>(visszavezet \/ elemzi az el\u0151zm\u00e9nyeket)<\/em><\/p><p>The author decided to _______ her journey through the remote mountains in her latest memoir. <em>(\u00fajra bej\u00e1r \/ le\u00edrja az \u00fatj\u00e1t)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">visszamegy \/ visszak\u00f6vet \/ \u00fajra bej\u00e1r<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): el\u0151rehalad \/ folytatja \/ tov\u00e1bbmegy<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ one&#039;s steps = visszamegy a nyom\u00e1n (pl. He had to _______ his steps to find his lost wallet.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a path = \u00fajra bej\u00e1r egy utat (pl. They decided to _______ the path of their ancestors.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a journey = \u00fajra bej\u00e1r egy utaz\u00e1st (pl. The documentary will _______ the journey of the explorers.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ the events = visszak\u00f6veti az esem\u00e9nyeket (pl. Police are trying to _______ the events leading up to the accident.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>retrace<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>retrace<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: retrace one&#039;s steps \/ retrace a path \/ retrace a journey \/ retrace events<\/span><\/p><p>similar: go back over \/ track back \/ revisit \/ review<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: advance \/ proceed \/ continue<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"retrace","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#636